---
import '../styles/about-contact.css';

const notes = [
  ['AI & automation', 'I’ve been running language models locally with Ollama and wiring them into n8n workflows. I like seeing what happens when a model can look something up or hand a task to another tool.'],
  ['Systems & software', 'Linux is where I explore what happens underneath an application. Python, FastAPI and PostgreSQL are some of the tools I’ve used to connect the pieces above it.'],
  ['Creative technology', 'I’m interested in how a web page can tell a story. Lately I’ve been exploring scroll-driven motion, interactive interfaces and the point where an experiment starts to feel good to use.'],
];
---

<section id="about" class="author-page" aria-labelledby="author-title">
  <div class="content author-spread">
    <figure class="author-print">
      <img src="/art/aditya.webp" width="680" height="907" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Aditya Dugar" />
      <figcaption>Aditya Dugar</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="author-notes">
      <h2 id="author-title">A little about me.</h2>
      <p>I’m studying Software Engineering at Jain University. Give me an unfamiliar app or a Linux machine and I’ll probably spend the afternoon figuring out what happens under the hood.</p>
      <p>During my internship at <strong>GrooveIt</strong>, I worked on backend development, authentication and debugging. Reading other people’s code taught me to ask better questions about my own.</p>
      <h3>In my notebook lately</h3>
      <div class="author-index">
        {notes.map(([title, text]) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{title}<span class="author-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <p>{text}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
